# Mileage — environment template. Copy to `.env` and fill in what you need.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# Everything here is OPTIONAL. With an empty .env the app runs fully offline
# (curated charts/ratios, aggregator fixtures, cached fares). Keys only upgrade
# data quality or turn on multi-user / Redis. `.env` is gitignored; never commit
# real secrets. Values are read from the process environment, so shell `export`
# still works too — .env is just the convenient local place to keep them.

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
# Core / local (Phase 0–4)
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
# SQLite file for durable truth (edges, runs, users, quota). Default: mileage.db
# MILEAGE_DB=mileage.db

# Disable the aggregator (Engine A) — set to any non-empty value to turn it off.
# MILEAGE_NO_AGGREGATOR=

# Comma-separated providers to disable (e.g. "aggregator,amadeus").
# MILEAGE_DISABLE_PROVIDERS=

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
# Live data providers (optional upgrades; absence degrades gracefully)
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
# Amadeus Self-Service — live L2 cash fares (the "price to beat").
# Without these, fares fall back to Travelpayouts cache -> curated hardcoded.
# Get free keys: https://developers.amadeus.com/  (My Apps -> Self-Service)
# AMADEUS_CLIENT_ID=
# AMADEUS_CLIENT_SECRET=

# seats.aero Partner API — OPTIONAL paid L3 award-space upgrade. Off by default;
# the aggregator is the default award-space source. Wired behind the interface.
# SEATS_AERO_API_KEY=

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
# Phase 4 — multi-user + shared memory layer
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
# Turn on per-user auth: the bearer token IS the user id; balances load from the
# Repository (server-side truth), not the request body. Unset/0/false = off.
# MILEAGE_AUTH=1

# Redis / Upstash — shared hot cache + global quota counter + de-dupe locks.
# Needs the extra:  pip install -e ".[multiuser]"
# If unreachable, the app logs a warning and falls back to in-process stores.
#
# Local Redis:
#   MILEAGE_REDIS_URL=redis://localhost:6379/0
#
# Upstash (TLS) — copy the "redis://"/"rediss://" URL from the Upstash console
# (Database -> Details -> Connect -> redis-cli / @upstash/redis URL). Use rediss://
# for the TLS endpoint:
#   MILEAGE_REDIS_URL=rediss://default:<UPSTASH_PASSWORD>@<region>-<name>.upstash.io:6379
# MILEAGE_REDIS_URL=

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
# Phase 5 — observability (Arize AX) + evals
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
# Each redemption run emits OpenInference spans (CHAIN `quote` -> RETRIEVER per
# provider -> verify -> optimize). Tracing is OPTIONAL + purely additive: with
# no deps/creds it is a no-op and the app runs unchanged. Needs the extra:
#   pip install -e ".[observability]"
#
# Ship spans to Arize AX:  https://app.arize.com -> Space Settings -> API keys
# ARIZE_SPACE_ID=
# ARIZE_API_KEY=
# ARIZE_PROJECT_NAME=mileage
#
# Local verification without an Arize account — print spans to the console:
# MILEAGE_TRACE_CONSOLE=1
#
# Force-disable tracing even if creds are present:
# MILEAGE_TRACE=0
#
# The golden-route evals (`mileage eval`) and the anti-hallucination gate need
# no config — they run offline and deterministically.

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
# Phase 8 — discovery intake (aggregator mode b): the mailbox feed (§6.1)
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
# `mileage discover` polls the inbox, takes each unread body as a document, and
# runs it through the LOCAL deterministic extractor (keyless — no Anthropic, no
# cloud, no model download). Auth is IMAP App Password ONLY: no Gmail API, no
# OAuth, no Pub/Sub. With these unset, discovery reads the bundled .eml fixtures
# so the pipeline still runs and is testable offline.
#   1. Enable 2-Step Verification on the Google account.
#   2. Create an App Password: https://myaccount.google.com/apppasswords
#   3. Paste the 16-character password (no spaces) into GMAIL_APP_PASSWORD.
# GMAIL_ADDRESS=occulosequor@gmail.com
# GMAIL_APP_PASSWORD=

# Optional active web search for discovery (NOT required):
# BING_SEARCH_API_KEY=
# SERPAPI_API_KEY=

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
# Offline / deterministic mode
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
# Pin the aggregator to its file:// fixtures (no live HTTP, no Wayback). The
# test suite sets this automatically so the suite is hermetic and never hangs on
# a blocked network; set it by hand to force a fully offline run.
# MILEAGE_OFFLINE=1
